course: dictionary
lesson: 9391
title: The springbok, a leaping antelope
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A springbok is a small, fast antelope from southern Africa. An antelope is a deer-like animal, and springboks are brown and white. Their name comes from their famous high jumps.
explain: Read the context: «Springboks and some gazelles leap high with stiff legs, called pronking or stotting.» The clues leap high and stiff legs show that this word names an animal that jumps. Pronking is the name for that jump.
explain: The same word can name a team. When you see «the Springboks» with a capital S and rugby words nearby, it means South Africa's national rugby team. The team is named after the animal. Always check the clues: capital letters and the topic tell you which meaning fits.
fact: A springbok is a small, fast antelope of southern Africa.
fact: «Springbok» names an animal, and it can also name a rugby team.
fact: «Pronking» means leaping straight up with stiff legs.
fact: The Springboks are the national rugby union team of South Africa.
fact: The springbok is a national symbol of South Africa.
exercise: What kind of animal is a springbok? | *A small, fast antelope | A bird that cannot fly | A large grey elephant | A fish with fins
exercise: «Springboks and some gazelles leap high with stiff legs, called pronking.» What does pronking mean? | Sleeping in the sun | Eating grass slowly | *Leaping straight up with stiff legs | Running in a circle
exercise: In «the Springboks won the rugby match», what do the Springboks mean? | *A famous national rugby team | Two small antelopes | A kind of grass | A herd of wild animals
test: Which country's national rugby team is called the Springboks? | Australia | England | *South Africa | New Zealand
test: In the sentence about pronking, what does the jump seem to tell a predator? | *I am fit, don't bother | I am lost, please help | I am asleep | I am hungry, come here
exam: Which clue tells you that «Springboks» names a team and not an animal? | the | *a capital S with rugby talk nearby | tonight | play
